# SG-Definition (Concept)
{ set { "SG-Definition" <id> <SG-Definition>
      "Spectral Gap" <name> <SG-Definition>
      "concept" <entity_type> <SG-Definition>
      "spectral-theory" <category> <SG-Definition>
      "spectral-gaps" <subcategory> <SG-Definition>
      "For a connected k-regular graph G with adjacency matrix A, the spectral gap\nis λ₂ = the second-largest eigenvalue of A (or equivalently: λ₂ = k - λ_{|V|-1}\nof the Laplacian L = kI - A).\nSpectral gap measures how quickly random walks mix on G.\n" <definition> <SG-Definition>
      "expander" <tags> <SG-Definition>
      "mixing-time" <tags> <SG-Definition>
      "alon-boppana" <tags> <SG-Definition>
      "laplacian" <tags> <SG-Definition>
      "expander" <tags> <SG-Definition>
      "mixing-time" <tags> <SG-Definition>
      "alon-boppana" <tags> <SG-Definition>
      "laplacian" <tags> <SG-Definition>
      "SG-Definition" <dgraph.type> "Concept" } }


# SG-Cheeger (Concept)
{ set { "SG-Cheeger" <id> <SG-Cheeger>
      "Cheeger Constant" <name> <SG-Cheeger>
      "concept" <entity_type> <SG-Cheeger>
      "spectral-theory" <category> <SG-Cheeger>
      "spectral-gaps" <subcategory> <SG-Cheeger>
      "h(G) = min_{S⊂V, |S|≤|V|/2} (e(S,V\\S) / |S|) where e(S,T) is the number of edges\nbetween S and T.\nThe Cheeger inequality: (λ₂/2) ≤ h(G) ≤ √(2λ₂) for k=4-regular graphs.\n" <definition> <SG-Cheeger>
      "cheeger" <tags> <SG-Cheeger>
      "isoperimetric" <tags> <SG-Cheeger>
      "inequality" <tags> <SG-Cheeger>
      "cheeger" <tags> <SG-Cheeger>
      "isoperimetric" <tags> <SG-Cheeger>
      "inequality" <tags> <SG-Cheeger>
      "SG-Cheeger" <dgraph.type> "Concept" } }


# SG-Alon-Boppana (Concept)
{ set { "SG-Alon-Boppana" <id> <SG-Alon-Boppana>
      "Alon-Boppana Bound" <name> <SG-Alon-Boppana>
      "concept" <entity_type> <SG-Alon-Boppana>
      "spectral-theory" <category> <SG-Alon-Boppana>
      "spectral-gaps" <subcategory> <SG-Alon-Boppana>
      "For any infinite family of k-regular graphs, the spectral gap satisfies\nlim sup λ₂ ≥ 2√(k-1).\nFor k=4: λ₂ ≥ 2√3 ≈ 3.464 for infinitely many graphs in any infinite family.\n" <definition> <SG-Alon-Boppana>
      "lower-bound" <tags> <SG-Alon-Boppana>
      "infinite-family" <tags> <SG-Alon-Boppana>
      "ramanujan" <tags> <SG-Alon-Boppana>
      "lower-bound" <tags> <SG-Alon-Boppana>
      "infinite-family" <tags> <SG-Alon-Boppana>
      "ramanujan" <tags> <SG-Alon-Boppana>
      "SG-Alon-Boppana" <dgraph.type> "Concept" } }


