# TO-Mayer1991 (Concept)
{ set { "TO-Mayer1991" <id> <TO-Mayer1991>
      "Mayer's Transfer Operator" <name> <TO-Mayer1991>
      "concept" <entity_type> <TO-Mayer1991>
      "dynam-systems" <category> <TO-Mayer1991>
      "transfer-operator" <subcategory> <TO-Mayer1991>
      "L_s : B(V) → B(V) (bounded operators on the Banach space of bounded functions)\nL_s f(x) = Σ_{n=1}^∞ (n+x)^{-2s} f(1/(n+x))\nwhere x ∈ (0,∞), s ∈ ℂ, and V is a suitable Banach space.\nThis is a weighted Perron-Frobenius-type operator.\n" <definition> <TO-Mayer1991>
      "For Re(s) > 1, L_s is nuclear (trace-class) on suitable spaces" <properties> <TO-Mayer1991>
      "For Re(s) > 1/2, L_s is compact" <properties> <TO-Mayer1991>
      "The negative exponent -2s is CRUCIAL — this distinguishes it from classical PF" <properties> <TO-Mayer1991>
      "transfer-operator" <tags> <TO-Mayer1991>
      "mayer" <tags> <TO-Mayer1991>
      "negative-exponent" <tags> <TO-Mayer1991>
      "transfer-operator" <tags> <TO-Mayer1991>
      "mayer" <tags> <TO-Mayer1991>
      "negative-exponent" <tags> <TO-Mayer1991>
      "TO-Mayer1991" <dgraph.type> "Concept" } }


