{ set { "FS-ML-Hecke-Traces-R2-0.73-0.99" <id> <FS-ML-Hecke-Traces-R2-0.73-0.99>
      "sklearn ML on LMFDB Hecke traces achieves R2 0.73-0.99" <name> <FS-ML-Hecke-Traces-R2-0.73-0.99>
      "finding" <entity_type> <FS-ML-Hecke-Traces-R2-0.73-0.99>
      "machine-learning" <category> <FS-ML-Hecke-Traces-R2-0.73-0.99>
      "ml-hecke" <subcategory> <FS-ML-Hecke-Traces-R2-0.73-0.99>
      "Exp 12 Thread B" <experiment> <FS-ML-Hecke-Traces-R2-0.73-0.99>
      "Exp Evidence-C" <experiment> <FS-ML-Hecke-Traces-R2-0.73-0.99>
      "2026-06-16" <date> <FS-ML-Hecke-Traces-R2-0.73-0.99>
      "{\"model\": \"sklearn - various models including Ridge, RandomForest, GradientBoosting, XGBoost\", \"features\": \"Hecke traces themselves a_2, a_3, a_5, a_7 ... up to a_m\", \"target\": \"z1 - first Hecke eigenvalue\", \"data_source\": \"LMFDB - 53044 newforms of weight 2, levels <= 2000\", \"split\": {\"stratified\": \"by dimension 1 to 20 and level\", \"cross-level\": \"train on levels < 1000, test on levels > 1000\"}}" <configuration> <FS-ML-Hecke-Traces-R2-0.73-0.99>
      "{\"stratified_split\": {\"gnn_gat_r2\": 0.731, \"sklearn_ridge_r2\": 0.812, \"sklearn_rf_r2\": 0.915, \"sklearn_xgb_r2\": 0.99, \"baseline_mean_r2\": 0.0, \"baseline_linear_r2\": 0.15, \"baseline_linear_note\": \"naive Hecke relations\"}, \"cross_level_split\": {\"gnn_gat_r2\": 0.53, \"sklearn_ridge_r2\": 0.556, \"sklearn_rf_r2\": null, \"sklearn_xgb_r2\": null, \"note\": \"Cross-level is harder - data quantity is the bottleneck\"}}" <results> <FS-ML-Hecke-Traces-R2-0.73-0.99>
      "{\"key_insight\": \"Side Information Does NOT Help. GNNs with rich graph features do NOT\\noutperform sklearn on Hecke traces alone. Hecke traces are a BAG OF FEATURES\\n- the per-prime identity is irrelevant. The graph structure helps moderately\\nover MLP baseline, but enriching node features with number theory does not improve.\\n\", \"conclusion\": \"Data quantity, not model architecture, was the bottleneck.\\nsklearn on Hecke traces succeeds because there are ENOUGH samples\\n(53k newforms) to learn statistical patterns.\\n\", \"data_insight\": \"Hecke traces are statistically self-similar - each trace a_p for prime p\\nis a normally-distributed random variable under Sato-Tate (for CM forms,\\nGUE distribution; for non-CM, a different distribution). ML learns these\\nstatistical regularities.\\n\"}" <analysis> <FS-ML-Hecke-Traces-R2-0.73-0.99>
      "confirmed" <status> <FS-ML-Hecke-Traces-R2-0.73-0.99>
      "very-high" <confidence> <FS-ML-Hecke-Traces-R2-0.73-0.99>
      "ml" <tags> <FS-ML-Hecke-Traces-R2-0.73-0.99>
